From: mscharged-port
Subject: Try one fallback graphics backend; let the caller report a failure
Upstream-base: d664382f57002fbff143911c81b06b7e7a4b3ab4

0091 made a failed explicit backend abort inside aurora_initialize, so a
player whose graphics driver Dawn rejects (Intel Vulkan on Windows below
driver 101.2111) got a crash report instead of the reason. The caller now
gets a null window and explains the failure itself. AuroraConfig gains
fallbackBackend: one other backend tried after the desired one fails (the
game's "auto" setting tries DirectX 12 after Vulkan); an explicit choice
without it still never switches.

diff --git a/include/aurora/aurora.h b/include/aurora/aurora.h
index 30338f7..e6eef05 100644
--- a/include/aurora/aurora.h
+++ b/include/aurora/aurora.h
@@ -125,6 +125,14 @@ typedef struct {
    * legacy preparation of every remembered/bundled configuration.
    */
   bool automaticPipelinePreparation;
+
+  /**
+   * Tried once when the explicit desiredBackend cannot start (no supported
+   * adapter, device or surface). BACKEND_AUTO, the zero default, tries no other
+   * backend. aurora_initialize reports the backend that started; when none
+   * did, it returns a null window and the errors are in the log.
+   */
+  AuroraBackend fallbackBackend;
 } AuroraConfig;
 
 typedef struct {
